# Hello, world

This is the first post on the new version of the blog. Posts are plain text files written in [Djot](https://djot.net), and a small Node script turns them into HTML.

Here is a short code sample, highlighted at build time:

{cap="Binary search over a sorted array"}
```js
function binarySearch(items, target) {
  let lo = 0;
  let hi = items.length - 1;
  while (lo <= hi) {
    const mid = (lo + hi) >> 1;
    if (items[mid] === target) return mid;
    if (items[mid] < target) lo = mid + 1;
    else hi = mid - 1;
  }
  return -1;
}
```

::: note
Notes, warnings and questions are rendered as callouts. Use `::: warn` or `::: quiz` for the other kinds.
:::

To start a new post, run `npm run new -- your-slug`. It creates a dated file in `content/posts`.
